  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Riviera Vet, on route du Plan de la Tour in Sainte-Maxime, is organised into two neighbouring entities: RivieraDOG for dogs, at 100 route du Plan de la Tour, opposite Maxibazar, and RivieraCAT for cats, at no. 98, behind Marie Blachère. The website mentions free, easy parking at both. For dog owners, RivieraDOG is the clinic that sees dogs: the site describes a reassuring environment with separate, adapted spaces, modern equipment for quick diagnoses and a multidisciplinary team.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>RivieraDOG is open Monday to Friday from 9am to 7pm and Saturday from 9am to 5pm; RivieraCAT is open Monday to Friday from 9am to 7pm, and on Saturday cats are seen at the RivieraDOG clinic. Appointments are booked online (separate links for dogs and cats) or by phone on 04 94 49 24 99. The clinic is Cat Friendly accredited.</p>
      <p>The care offered for dogs includes orthopaedic surgery, soft-tissue surgery, medical imaging and nutrition. More broadly, the site lists abdominal ultrasound, echocardiography, endoscopy, geriatric, preventive, internal and general medicine, hospitalisation, emergencies, ophthalmology, reproduction, oncology, dermatology and osteopathy by appointment.</p>
      <p>The site also gives sample prices, to be confirmed at the clinic: consultation €49, dog vaccination consultation from €63, male dog neutering from €269 and spaying from €377.</p>
      <p>In an emergency outside consultation hours, the site refers you to the Centre Urgence Vétérinaire Delta 83 in Puget-sur-Argens, on 04 89 88 34 34: the clinic does not announce an on-site night service.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: book at RivieraDOG for your dog (the clinic that sees dogs) and keep 04 89 88 34 34 handy for out-of-hours emergencies.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Sainte-Maxime and its seafront are close by; dog rules on the town's beaches vary with the season, so check on site.</p>
